---
description: Rules for the embedded web interface — English only, static landing page, no build step
globs: internal/ui/web/**
alwaysApply: false
---

# English only

Everything under `internal/ui/web/static` is English — markup, UI strings and comments in
CSS and JS. `TestStaticFilesAreEnglish` scans the whole embedded tree for Cyrillic.

# The landing page stays static

`index.html` carries exactly one script: `static/js/contact.js`, for the contact dialog.
Everything else is static markup, because search and AI crawlers usually do not execute
JavaScript — content built by a script does not exist for them.
`TestLandingScriptsAreLimitedToContactForm` guards this.

# No build step

- Vue and PrimeVue load as ES modules through an `importmap` on the tools page. The version
  is pinned in two places and both must match, or `provide/inject` inside PrimeVue breaks
  silently.
- PrimeVue runs against the runtime build without a template compiler: components are
  written with `render()`/`h()`, not string templates.
- Numbers and dates go through `static/js/format.js` — `en-US` numbers, `en-GB` dates with a
  spelled-out month. Do not introduce a second convention.
- Colours come from the CSS variables in `static/css/app.css`; charts repeat the same palette
  by value, since Chart.js cannot read CSS variables.

# Tested invariants

Paths inside embedded files are strings: a typo compiles and only breaks in the browser.
`pages_test.go` checks that every `/static/...` reference exists, that the canonical host is
consistent, that `/tools` stays `noindex`, that structured data matches the visible text and
that form limits equal the contract's. Extend those tests when adding a page or an asset.

Details: `.ai/conventions.md`.
